fold to any bet. But checking risks giving a free card to opponent’s weaker draw.  \n\nMost sensible for pot control with only 1 card to come is to check and hope to hit flush on river, then value bet.  \n\n**Reason:**  \nMy hand has little showdown value now, but strong draw potential (flush draw). In position with a checked-to turn, taking a free river is acceptable. Raising might get called by better hands (Jx, 2x, overpairs) and fold out worse, which doesn’t help. Worse hands that call are mostly other draws that might outdraw me anyway.  \nChecking keeps variance low and preserves stack for later hands.  \n\n**Answer:** 0'}
